    "--format",
    "json",
    "Complete this repository task: `suggestSimilar(word, candidates)` currently only recognises an exact match, so a mistyped\ncommand or flag produces no 'did you mean' hint. Implement real similarity matching in\n`lib/suggestSimilar.js`.\n\nRequirements:\n- compare `word` against `candidates` using an edit distance that also counts a transposition of\n  two adjacent characters as a single edit;\n- only consider candidates within 3 edits, and reject any whose similarity, measured as\n  (length - distance) / length against the longer of the two strings, is not greater than 0.4;\n- candidates of one character or shorter are never suggested;\n- keep only the closest candidates: a strictly better distance discards previous matches, an\n  equal distance joins them;\n- de-duplicate candidates, and sort the surviving suggestions with localeCompare;\n- when `word` starts with '--', compare without the leading dashes but restore them in the output;\n- return '' when nothing qualifies, '\\n(Did you mean X?)' for one match, and\n  '\\n(Did you mean one of A, B?)' for several;\n- return '' when candidates is empty, null or undefined.\nWork only in the current repository. Do not push, open a PR, deploy, or access secrets.\nMake the smallest correct change and run relevant local checks."
  ],
